{"id":"chatcmpl-f67ffe96-525c-4873-9c98-a9d04b57edc8","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244473,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: querying multiple independent vision-language models with anatomically-framed questions to resolve laterality ambiguity. The key insight is that lateral views require explicit anatomical reasoning to map findings to the correct side, and agreement across independent tools increases confidence. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where spatial orientation or laterality is ambiguous.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a visual finding's laterality is ambiguous (e.g., lateral views), query multiple independent models with anatomically-framed questions rather than relying on a single interpretation.\",\n    \"Decompose the diagnostic question into a location/laterality sub-question first, then cross-validate with a second tool using different reasoning framing.\",\n    \"Use agreement between independent tools as a confidence signal before committing to a final answer.\",\n    \"Frame tool queries with explicit anatomical context (view type, expected landmarks) to elicit more reliable spatial reasoning.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"For lateral or ambiguous views, explicitly ask about anatomical landmarks (e.g., costophrenic angle) and require the model to map findings to a side using standard view anatomy.\",\n    \"Multi-tool visual reasoning\": \"Query at least two independent models with differently-phrased but equivalent questions; treat convergent answers as higher-confidence evidence.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality disambiguation\": \"Separate 'what is the finding' from 'which side is it on' into distinct queries, since models often handle these with different reliability.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the imaging view type (e.g., lateral vs. PA) before interpreting laterality, since lateral views require anatomical mapping.\",\n    \"Verify that independent tools agree on the finding and its side before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":469,"total_tokens":855,"completion_tokens":386,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":469},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":386}}}